WEBVTT

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.300
Lord Reinhard.

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:42.890
Lord Reinhard.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:48.890
Awake !

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:50.450
Awake !

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:52.890
Awake !

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:54.890
Awake !

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:56.520
Awake !

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:58.610
Awake !

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:01.030
Awake !

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:03.550
Awake !

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:24.960
Dreams of the Morning, Songs of the Night

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:24.960
Chapter 2

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:34.210
I had a dream.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:38.800
We'd already graduated
and fought on the front lines.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:40.510
We fought many times and won.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:44.500
We destroyed an enemy base.

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:47.150
We destroyed a cruiser
with a destroyer.

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:54.360
We almost died several times,
but together, we escaped the danger.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.600
That wasn't a
dream, Lord Reinhard.

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:01.590
The reason we're back at school is because we
have been given an assignment by the MPs.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:06.150
Assignment ?

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:07.760
The Military Police ?

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:11.770
Form a line.

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:12.530
Count off !

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:14.450
One.{Eins.}

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:15.520
Two.{Zwei.}

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:16.480
Three.{Drei.}

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:17.490
Four.{Vier.}

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:18.490
Five.{Funf.}

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:19.410
Six.{Sechs.}

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:20.310
Seven.{Sieben.}

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:21.390
Eight.{Acht.}

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:22.050
Nine.{Neun.}

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:18.890
Usually, I prefer not to let in outsiders,
but the situation being what it is...

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:21.400
In order to
restore our honor...

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:26.500
...we must solve this incident and let
the unfortunate student rest in peace.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:32.400
As investigators and graduates of
this school, I'll rely on your efforts.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:36.530
But you delayed reporting to
the MPs too much for that...

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:46.400
Do you think it's an Alliance ploy, killing
a student in an Imperial military school ?

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:53.000
If so, the Alliance might have
the ability to travel through time.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.650
They might target...

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:58.710
...the Ministry of Military Affairs.

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:05.780
Rather than blaming
it on the Alliance...

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:09.180
...is it not possible to think that
there might be fraud at this school...

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:14.180
...and he was killed because
he found out about it ?

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:19.740
This is an example,
just an example, Mr. Principal.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:24.070
If I offended you, I apologize for
speaking of these matters lightly.

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:29.790
I can no longer think of things honestly
after being in the MPs for a while.

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:34.550
If you think it's necessary, you
should check the school records.

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:38.720
I don't think you will find
anything wrong with them.

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:42.150
No, that won't
be necessary.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.240
There is no
need to hesitate.

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:45.880
You should check them.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:56.620
They will eventually head to the
battlefield, and fight against the Alliance.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:08:01.580
But it's unfortunate that these
students must be questioned.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:04.560
I apologize, Principal.

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:06.890
But you said "questioned."

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:09.700
I thought it was not
reported publicly as murder

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:15.390
Rumor is faster than light
and smaller than a particle.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.100
No matter how hard we try,
we cannot stop it from spreading.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:23.240
I see.

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:27.040
But I don't want you to
question the students randomly.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:31.260
I will have a dependable
student cooperate with you.

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:36.700
So I want you to get over
this unfortunate incident...

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:42.400
...and I hope that you will continue to
put your full effort into your studies.

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:14.090
This is where the unfortunate
incident happened.

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:44.740
I guess there's no way any
physical evidence is left.

00:09:44.740 --> 00:09:46.330
I agree.

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:51.550
We should look at the
MP's report for the details.

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:52.350
I agree.

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:08.450
Are there any rumors about this
incident circulating in the school ?

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:09.560
Yes, sir.

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:12.720
People are saying
it might be a curse.

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:14.200
Curse ?

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:15.610
Yes, sir.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:21.650
People say that a student who died of an accident in the past wants more people to die like him.

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:26.790
Or Reifeisen saw a gathering of
devil worshippers, and was killed.

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:28.490
There are many
rumors like that.

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:32.250
Thank you for your valuable opinion.

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:45.190
My shoulders get stiff
when he acts that politely.

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:48.160
He used to scold us back in
the days when we were students.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:49.150
True.

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:52.200
But they're saying it's a curse ?

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.640
This is a school.

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:57.150
There must be
some spooky stories.

00:10:57.150 --> 00:11:00.020
You didn't like
spooky stories, did you ?

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:05.410
You were the one who hid
in a fortress made of blankets...

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:07.770
...because you were
afraid of the dark.

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:09.520
We did that together.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:12.300
Anyway, that was back in
the days when we were small.

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:17.020
We can't blame this crime on a monster
who is hiding in the dark any more.

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:27.600
I guess that's the same mentality as the principal who blames everything on the Alliance.

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:31.390
It's not like you to say 
such harsh things of others.

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:33.250
But you're totally right.

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:40.720
If they could do that, they'd sneak into Neue Sansouci and kill the Kaiser in his sleep.

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:43.110
Lord Reinhard.

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:45.350
It's OK.

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:46.910
No one is listening.

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:49.460
I do choose my time and place
when saying things like that.

00:11:49.460 --> 00:11:52.690
That's why I changed it to 
"Bureau of Military Affairs" last time.

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:05.690
If we walk around, we might
run into some new information.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:08.850
And there is no need
worry about eavesdroppers.

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:13.040
You worry too much.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:13.840
Thanks to you.

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.060
You...

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:25.850
Therefore...

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:35.690
This is Eckhardt's
biological theory.

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:38.870
We know so far that...

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:42.130
Things are getting older.

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:44.460
Not only the buildings,
but the people as well.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:50.420
Rather than giving birth to something
new, they emphasize tradition...

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:52.800
...and make people believe
that tradition is always right.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.850
That kind of education
is being taught here.

00:12:57.620 --> 00:13:02.500
Those who search for something new are thought to be people who disturb the order in this place.

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:03.600
This is ridiculous.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:09.180
Of course, it is true that unchanging
scenes bring back memories.

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:12.690
Yes, the library
hasn't changed a bit.

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:17.710
We fought with the
upperclassmen down that hall.

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:18.730
It was 4 on 2.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:19.770
Yes.

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:24.060
We often had disputes with the upperclassmen until we became upperclassmen.

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:27.830
There were always a lot of them,
but there were only two of us.

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:36.830
I threw the upperclassmen who spoke
ill of my elder sister in that fountain.

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:40.160
This was a
small battlefield.

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:43.690
There are many signs
of your accomplishments.

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:49.950
Don't speak of it as if it
has nothing to do with you.

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:57.050
We only graduated 2 years ago,
but if it weren't for you...

00:13:57.050 --> 00:14:02.040
...I would have entered
the underworld 5 or 6 times.

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:07.000
Did you know this ?

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:15.140
You have a ticket to the underworld but do not have the ticket for entry into the underworld.

00:14:16.010 --> 00:14:19.150
So you cannot die, even
in a dangerous situation.

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:22.430
Really ?

00:14:22.430 --> 00:14:23.860
I didn't know that.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:25.570
That's a convenient story.

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:09.280
This is good.

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:10.890
Let's look at the data over there.

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:20.230
What kind of grades
did the victim have ?

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:26.270
His rank went up and down
between 10th and 50th in the class.

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:32.600
So we can say he was an excellent
student, but not outstanding.

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:36.740
It doesn't seem like he was
killed because of his grades.

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:40.350
At any rate, what was he
doing in the food warehouse ?

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:46.100
The fact that he left the dormitory in the
middle of the night is weird to start with.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:50.880
If everyone follows
the rules, yes.

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:53.460
You're right.

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:56.060
It was not like
we didn't do that.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:57.790
There are some
nonsensical rules.

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:01.930
Like the angle of your feet
when you salute the flag...

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:04.770
...and that underwear
must be white, and so on.

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:11.190
It's so stupid that even the rules that must be obeyed are starting to be looked down upon.

00:16:12.710 --> 00:16:13.790
Yes.

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:17.420
We can understand that Reifeisen
snuck out of the dormitory.

00:16:17.420 --> 00:16:21.830
Do you think the reason he snuck into
the warehouse was to steal food ?

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:24.910
It seems that he complained 
of the cafeteria food fairly often.

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:29.770
I can understand that complaint.

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:33.020
I ate cafeteria food for
the first time in a while.

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:36.670
The amount was acceptable,
but it tasted horrible.

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:40.030
It hasn't changed since
the time we were here.

00:16:40.030 --> 00:16:44.450
But that isn't enough of
a reason to be attacked.

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:49.600
When we complained, the
principal used to say to us...

00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:52.360
"We think thoroughly
about the nutrition."

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:56.050
"It's a sign of weakness if one
who fights for the Empire..."

00:16:56.050 --> 00:17:00.450
"...complains about the food's
taste and asks for gourmet food."

00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:03.310
That's just like him.

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:04.590
We heard that one a lot.

00:17:05.950 --> 00:17:10.370
But when high ranking people order
lower ranking people to conserve...

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:13.690
...it is rare that the higher
ranking people do as he orders.

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:16.960
Although Rudolf said
"obesity is evidence of laziness"...

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:24.840
...and promoted a simple diet, he himself was a gourmand, and suffered gout in his late years.

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:32.030
Even the previous principal hid
fine wine and caviar in his cabinet.

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:35.300
I wonder if the current principal, 
Principal Steger, does anything like that.

00:17:35.300 --> 00:17:36.640
Who knows ?

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:39.980
But I didn't hear any bad rumors
of him when we were in school.

00:17:39.980 --> 00:17:44.270
At the very least, I wasn't
treated unfairly by him.

00:17:44.270 --> 00:17:45.790
Surprising, isn't it ?

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:46.910
Yes.

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:48.260
Let's get back
to the business.

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:52.340
You said steal food, but they
only keep dry stores there.

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:55.360
You can't eat those unless
they're properly prepared.

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:56.090
You're right.

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:06.590
Excuse me, sir.

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:11.800
My name is Moritz
von Haase, a senior.

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:17.750
I was sent by the principal to cooperate
with Captain Musel on the incident.

00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:19.410
Oh, thank you.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:20.740
Sit down.

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:24.090
No, I can't sit down
in front of you, Captain.

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:26.480
Please ask me
questions as I am.

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:29.960
Oh, fine then.

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:32.930
How do people assess
the late Reifeisen ?

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:34.370
I don't know too much.

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:38.510
Was there anyone in particular
who didn't get along with him ?

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:40.440
I don't know.

00:18:43.950 --> 00:18:46.160
Then, was there anyone who
got along with him well ?

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:47.420
I did.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:48.990
I see.

00:18:48.990 --> 00:18:52.730
Then, from your perspective,
what kind of person was Reifeisen ?

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:57.650
For example, when someone
got better grades than he did...

00:18:57.650 --> 00:19:01.270
...did he not care or
did he worry about that ?

00:19:01.270 --> 00:19:03.160
Stuff like that.

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:05.250
If I think about it, he
did worry about that often.

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:07.390
Did he have the tendency to
blame everything on others ?

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:09.190
A tendency to blame others ?

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:14.420
For example, did he blame his
faults on others from time to time ?

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:17.990
Yes, he did that
from time to time.

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:20.850
You don't defend him even
though he was your friend ?

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:26.700
I think that it is best to answer
you honestly for the investigation.

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:33.300
It seems to me that he is
saying what people want to hear...

00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:36.040
...rather than what
he thinks or believes.

00:19:40.520 --> 00:19:41.870
Who scored ?

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:45.100
The team not in yellow.

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:53.360
Thank you.

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:53.910
You may go.

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:05.400
He was a useless guy.

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:09.090
It's not that he
wasn't cooperating.

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:12.500
It seems like he doesn't really care
much about people's relationships.

00:20:13.460 --> 00:20:20.140
He probably feels reality in numbers
and letters and is a genius in that field.

00:20:20.140 --> 00:20:22.700
The type of person who
is useless in a real battle.

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:25.310
Why did the principal
send a person like him ?

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:29.600
He's at the
top of the class.

00:20:31.570 --> 00:20:35.310
That's why grades cannot
really measure people.

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:41.220
That sounds sarcastic coming from Lord
Reinhard, who was at the top of our class.

00:20:42.940 --> 00:20:47.160
For school work, all you have to do is to
memorize the main points and apply them.

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:50.380
Grades are useless.

00:20:50.380 --> 00:20:53.060
Anyway, we should get
back to the incident.

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:54.020
Right.

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:55.770
By the way, we haven't
found a murder weapon yet.

00:20:56.650 --> 00:21:00.310
How did they kill him and how
did they hide the weapon ?

00:21:01.220 --> 00:21:04.890
That's important, too, but we
should think about the motive.

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:11.150
Although that only
boils down to one thing.

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:12.670
You know what that is,
right, Kircheis ?

00:21:13.430 --> 00:21:15.520
The question of how do they
benefit from the crime, right ?

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:16.790
Right.

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:18.800
It's just like war.

00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:22.750
The only difference
is how it appears.

00:21:22.750 --> 00:21:27.020
Do you aggressively try to win or hold
everything as it is to minimize the loss ?

00:21:27.020 --> 00:21:31.430
The motive can be divided into
offensive and defensive motives, but...

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:37.070
We might need to think
about revenge as a motive.

00:21:37.670 --> 00:21:41.770
In a broad sense, that is
a defensive motive, though.

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:43.160
What's wrong ?

00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:48.050
I figured out the reason
why we were sent here.

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:49.110
Why did they ?

00:21:49.110 --> 00:21:51.850
To make the
criminal careless.

00:21:51.850 --> 00:21:53.570
I see.

00:21:53.570 --> 00:21:59.750
I heard that the principal was furious when
he heard that the MPs were sending us...

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:03.490
...because he thought that they
weren't taking this incident seriously.

00:22:03.490 --> 00:22:07.100
He acted that way
to my face, though.

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:09.710
I don't care
what they think...

00:22:09.710 --> 00:22:13.540
...but I hope that the criminal will be
careless and leave us some evidence.

00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:15.280
I wonder.

00:22:24.630 --> 00:22:29.000
In this way, the second day
of the investigation ended.

00:22:29.720 --> 00:22:34.650
The funeral for Reifeisen
was scheduled for tomorrow...

00:22:34.650 --> 00:22:37.800
...but the investigation
still lacked any direction.

00:22:36.050 --> 00:22:39.200
To be continued

00:22:42.400 --> 00:22:54.680
I don't wait to live a life of counting memories

00:22:42.800 --> 00:22:48.340
[ Long Relationship ]

00:22:42.800 --> 00:22:48.340
Ending Theme

00:22:42.800 --> 00:22:48.340
Vocals: Ogura Kei

00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:55.120
Reinhard:

00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:55.120
Horikawa Ryo

00:22:56.050 --> 00:23:08.600
But with you, I've had a long relationship...

00:22:56.350 --> 00:23:01.850
Steger:

00:22:56.350 --> 00:23:01.850
Fujimoto Yuzuru

00:23:10.550 --> 00:23:16.100
...and it feels as though the memories...

00:23:10.830 --> 00:23:16.340
Narrator:

00:23:10.830 --> 00:23:16.340
Yara Yuusaku

00:23:16.850 --> 00:23:23.470
...might get carried off somewhere

00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:23.240
Translation:
Toshiaki

00:23:23.240 --> 00:23:29.240
Timing:
Todd Perkins

00:23:23.470 --> 00:23:30.050
Maybe it's a momentary worry

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:35.250
Song Translation:
Toshiaki

00:23:30.750 --> 00:23:36.800
Thinking, "People change," I shake my head

00:23:35.250 --> 00:23:41.450
Editing:
Todd Perkins
Barbara
Dave
Brain
Mouse
Omar
Steve S.
